KNOWNBUG
main.cpp
--cpp17
^EXIT=6$
^SIGNAL=0$
^CONVERSION ERROR$
--
^warning: ignoring
^VERIFICATION
could not fully type-check
--
N5008 [over.match.class.deduct]/1, [over.match.copy]/1.1: in
copy-initialization the guide formed from an explicit constructor is not a
candidate, so `E e = 1;' has no viable deduction guide and the program is
ill-formed.  The front end does reject it, but only after deducing E<int>
(the error is "copy-initialization of 'struct E' from 'signed int' requires
an explicit constructor"), and the rejection is a dropped body of main
("could not fully type-check 'main'") rather than a plain diagnostic.  bin53
rejected it plainly ("found no match for symbol 'E'") and passes this test;
the dropped body comes from the copy-initialization check of ef2a71f448
running after deduction.  g++ 13 and clang++ 18 reject this program.
